<SiteLayout title="Terms of service — Agoca Labs" description="Terms governing use of the Agoca Labs website, personal automations, and creator-operated video-publishing workflow.">
<div class="policy-header wrap"><p class="eyebrow">TERMS OF SERVICE</p><h1>Useful tools.<br />Clear boundaries.</h1><p class="policy-date">Terms of service · Effective September 12, 2026</p><p>These terms govern access to the Agoca Labs website, personal automations, and creator-operated publishing tools.</p></div>
<div class="policy-layout wrap"><nav class="policy-nav" aria-label="Terms of service sections">{sections.map(([id,label])=><a href={'#'+id}>{label}</a>)}</nav><article class="policy-content">
<section id="agreement"><h2>01. Agreement to these terms</h2><p>By accessing or using an Agoca Labs service, you agree to these terms and the <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>. If you do not agree, do not use the service. Agoca Labs is an independent project operated by Agoca.</p></section>
<section id="services"><h2>02. The services</h2><p>Agoca Labs develops personal AI and automation tools. Current features may include email classification and summaries, Telegram-based controls and approvals, creation of English and Spanish short-form videos, and delivery of creator-approved videos to connected TikTok accounts.</p><p>The services are currently limited-access tools for accounts authorized by the operator. Public self-service registration is not offered. Features may be experimental, incomplete, or changed as the project develops.</p></section>
<section id="accounts"><h2>03. Connected accounts</h2><p>Some features require authorization to access third-party services such as Google, Telegram, or TikTok. You may connect only accounts you own or are authorized to administer. You are responsible for maintaining the security of those accounts and for activity performed through your authorization.</p><p>You may revoke a connection through the relevant third-party service or ask the operator to disconnect it. Revocation stops future access under that authorization but may not remove prior workflow records or content already delivered or published.</p></section>
<section id="content"><h2>04. Creator content and approvals</h2><p>You retain ownership of content you provide. You grant Agoca Labs a limited permission to process, format, store, transmit, upload, or publish that content only as needed to operate the requested workflow.</p><p>You are responsible for confirming that you have the rights and permissions needed for videos, images, audio, captions, trademarks, and other material submitted for processing or publication. A publishing approval instructs the workflow to send the approved version to the selected connected account. English and Spanish versions may have separate approval stages and may be published independently.</p><p>You remain responsible for reviewing content before approval and for posts made to connected accounts, including their accuracy, legality, disclosures, and compliance with TikTok's rules.</p></section>
<section id="use"><h2>05. Acceptable use</h2><p>Do not use the services to violate law, infringe intellectual-property or privacy rights, distribute malware, mislead people about the source of content, evade platform safeguards, access an account without authorization, or publish content prohibited by a connected service. Do not interfere with, reverse engineer, overload, or misuse the services.</p></section>
<section id="third-parties"><h2>06. Third-party services</h2><p>Google, Telegram, TikTok, Cloudflare, ngrok, and other providers operate under their own terms and policies. Agoca Labs does not control their availability, review decisions, account actions, content moderation, or changes to their APIs. Use of TikTok features is also subject to TikTok's applicable terms, community guidelines, and developer policies.</p></section>
<section id="availability"><h2>07. Availability and changes</h2><p>The services are provided on an evolving, limited-access basis. Agoca Labs may modify, suspend, limit, or discontinue features to maintain security, comply with law or platform requirements, address technical issues, or improve the project. No particular feature, publication time, or uninterrupted availability is guaranteed.</p></section>
<section id="disclaimers"><h2>08. Disclaimers and limitation of liability</h2><p>To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, the services are provided “as is” and “as available,” without warranties of uninterrupted operation, error-free output, fitness for a particular purpose, or non-infringement. Automated and AI-generated output may contain mistakes and must be reviewed before approval or use.</p><p>To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, Agoca Labs and its operator will not be liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages; loss of data, revenue, reputation, or opportunity; platform enforcement; or publication errors arising from use of or inability to use the services.</p></section>
<section id="changes"><h2>09. Termination and changes to these terms</h2><p>Access may be suspended or ended for misuse, security concerns, platform requirements, or discontinuation of a service. These terms may be updated as the project changes. The effective date identifies the current version; continued use after an update means you accept the revised terms.</p><p>If any provision is found unenforceable, the remaining provisions will continue to apply. These terms and the Privacy Policy form the agreement governing use of the services.</p></section>
<section id="contact"><h2>10. Contact</h2><p>For questions about these terms, connected accounts, or the services, email <a href="mailto:agomezcasarez@gmail.com">agomezcasarez@gmail.com</a>.</p></section>
</article></div></SiteLayout>
